IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc31-forms-periods`

-- ccc31-forms-orders.l4 -- Forms 46, 47, 48, 48.1 and 51 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the Probation Order, the Order
-- To Disclose Income Tax Information, the two Assessment Orders and the Notice of Obligation To Provide Samples of Bodily Substance.
-- Layer 1: the law as the Forms state it, from the text alone, from no one's point of view.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read a result (NOTES.md): MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the Form's words reach the case. JUST FALSE: the Form says no in its own words
-- (a period that has run or not begun, a "when" or "if" that fails, a bare "must" not done: fork F5). NOTHING: not covered (a premise not made
-- out, a limit of the grant, a seam answer that is not JUST TRUE). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seam inputs, named as PLAN.md section 4 and section 7 name them: `s 732.1(3) ...`, `s 2 newly-born child: ...` (MAYBE BOOLEAN).
-- Dates are `Date day month year`; a period is a `Length of time` counted by ccc31-forms-periods (it begins ON the day named: fork F16).
-- The minute of the day is a NUMBER of minutes after midnight (as the keel counts it in s 2 "day").

§ `Form 46 (Section 732.1) -- Probation Order`

-- src:18845 | FORM 46 (Section 732.1) Probation Order
-- src:18846 | Canada,
-- src:18847 | Province of ,
-- src:18848 | (territorial division).
-- src:18849 | Whereas on the day of at , A.B., hereinafter called the offender, (pleaded guilty to or was tried under (here insert Part XIX, XX or XXVII, as the case may be) of the Criminal Code and was (here insert convicted or found guilty, as the case may be) on the charge that (here state the offence to which the offender pleaded guilty or for which the offender was convicted or found guilty, as the case may be);
-- src:18850 | And whereas on the day of the court adjudged*
-- src:18851 | (a) that the offender be discharged on the following conditions:
-- src:18852 | (b) that the passing of sentence on the offender be suspended and that the said offender be released on the following conditions:
-- src:18853 | (c) that the offender forfeit and pay the sum of dollars to be applied according to law and in default of payment of the said sum without delay (or within a time fixed, if any), be imprisoned in the (prison) at for the term of unless the said sum and charges of the committal and of conveying the said offender to the said prison are sooner paid, and in addition thereto, that the said offender comply with the following conditions:
-- src:18854 | (d) that the offender be imprisoned in the (prison) at for the term of and, in addition thereto, that the said offender comply with the following conditions:
-- src:18855 | (e) that following the expiration of the offender’s conditional sentence order related to this or another offence, that the said offender comply with the following conditions:
-- src:18856 | (f) that following the expiration of the offender’s sentence of imprisonment related to another offence, that the said offender comply with the following conditions:
-- src:18857 | (g) when the offender is ordered to serve the sentence of imprisonment intermittently, that the said offender comply with the following conditions when not in confinement:
-- src:18858 | Now therefore the said offender shall, for the period of from the date of this order (or, where paragraph (d), (e) or (f) is applicable, the date of expiration of the offender’s sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order) comply with the following conditions, namely, that the said offender shall keep the peace and be of good behaviour, appear before the court when required to do so by the court and notify the court or probation officer in advance of any change of name or address and promptly notify the court or probation officer of any change of employment or occupation, and, in addition,
-- src:18859 | (here state any additional conditions prescribed pursuant to subsection 732.1(3) of the Criminal Code).
-- src:18860 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18861 | Clerk of the Court, Justice or Provincial Court Judge
@ref Form 46 (Section 732.1) (src:18845-18861)
DECLARE `form 46 the court's adjudication` IS ONE OF
    `form 46 (a) discharged on conditions`
    `form 46 (b) passing of sentence suspended and released on conditions`
    `form 46 (c) fine, imprisonment in default of payment, and conditions in addition`
    `form 46 (d) imprisoned and, in addition, conditions`
    `form 46 (e) conditions following the expiration of a conditional sentence order`
    `form 46 (f) conditions following the expiration of a sentence of imprisonment related to another offence`
    `form 46 (g) intermittent sentence, conditions when not in confinement`

-- "for the period of ___ from the date of this order (or, where paragraph (d), (e) or (f) is applicable, the date of expiration of the
-- offender's sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order)": the day the period of the conditions begins.
@ref Form 46 (Section 732.1) (src:18851-18858)
GIVEN adjudication IS A `form 46 the court's adjudication`
      `the date of this order` IS A DATE
      `the date of expiration of the offender's sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`form 46 the conditions begin on` MEANS
    CONSIDER adjudication
    WHEN `form 46 (d) imprisoned and, in addition, conditions` THEN `the date of expiration of the offender's sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order`
    WHEN `form 46 (e) conditions following the expiration of a conditional sentence order` THEN `the date of expiration of the offender's sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order`
    WHEN `form 46 (f) conditions following the expiration of a sentence of imprisonment related to another offence` THEN `the date of expiration of the offender's sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order`
    OTHERWISE `the date of this order`

-- The offender "shall, for the period of ___ from the date of this order ... comply with the following conditions": do the conditions bind
-- on the day? Outside the period: JUST FALSE (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)). Paragraph (g): the
-- conditions apply "when not in confinement": in confinement, JUST FALSE ("when" counts as "where", ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; fork F11).
@ref Form 46 (Section 732.1) (src:18857-18858)
GIVEN adjudication IS A `form 46 the court's adjudication`
      `the date of this order` IS A DATE
      `the date of expiration of the offender's sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order` IS A DATE
      period IS A `Length of time`
      `the offender is in confinement on the day asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 46 the offender must comply with the conditions on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the day asked about` (`form 46 the conditions begin on` adjudication `the date of this order` `the date of expiration of the offender's sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order`) period)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the period of from the date of this order (or, where paragraph (d), (e) or (f) is applicable, the date of expiration of the offender’s sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order) comply with the following conditions"
        IF adjudication EQUALS `form 46 (g) intermittent sentence, conditions when not in confinement` AND `the offender is in confinement on the day asked about`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the offender is ordered to serve the sentence of imprisonment intermittently, that the said offender comply with the following conditions when not in confinement"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The four standing conditions: "keep the peace and be of good behaviour, appear before the court when required to do so by the court and
-- notify the court or probation officer in advance of any change of name or address and promptly notify the court or probation officer of any
-- change of employment or occupation". The caller says, of each, whether it arose and whether it was done; "promptly" is a plain input
-- (the text fixes no period). Fork F12: a bare "shall" not done answers JUST FALSE (the duty is not met); the other reading is NOTHING.
@ref Form 46 (Section 732.1) (src:18858)
GIVEN `the offender has kept the peace and been of good behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has required the offender to appear` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender appeared before the court when required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender's name or address has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender notified the court or probation officer in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender's employment or occupation has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender notified the court or probation officer promptly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 46 the offender is in compliance with the standard conditions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender has kept the peace and been of good behaviour`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "keep the peace and be of good behaviour"
        IF `the court has required the offender to appear` AND NOT `the offender appeared before the court when required`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "appear before the court when required to do so by the court"
        IF `the offender's name or address has changed` AND NOT `the offender notified the court or probation officer in advance`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "notify the court or probation officer in advance of any change of name or address"
        IF `the offender's employment or occupation has changed` AND NOT `the offender notified the court or probation officer promptly`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "promptly notify the court or probation officer of any change of employment or occupation"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "(here state any additional conditions prescribed pursuant to subsection 732.1(3) of the Criminal Code)": whether a condition is one that
-- subsection prescribes is the answer of the part that owns it.
@ref Form 46 (Section 732.1) (src:18859)
GIVEN `s 732.1(3) the condition is one the court may prescribe under subsection 732.1(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 46 the additional condition may be stated` MEANS
    IF `s 732.1(3) the condition is one the court may prescribe under subsection 732.1(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any additional conditions prescribed pursuant to subsection 732.1(3)": what that subsection prescribes is its own part's answer

-- The four standing conditions as regulative rules (each takes the number of days within which it must be done; "promptly" and "in advance"
-- fix no number in the text, so the caller supplies one). A trace prints; it cannot be asserted on the stable binary.
DECLARE `form 46 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 46 breach the peace or misbehave`
    `form 46 appear before the court`
    `form 46 notify the court or probation officer of the change`

@ref Form 46 (Section 732.1) (src:18858)
GIVEN `the days in the period` IS A NUMBER
`form 46 the duty to keep the peace and be of good behaviour` MEANS
    PARTY `the offender`
    SHANT `form 46 breach the peace or misbehave`
    WITHIN `the days in the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the offender` BECAUSE "the offender did not keep the peace and be of good behaviour"

@ref Form 46 (Section 732.1) (src:18858)
GIVEN `the days within which the court requires the offender to appear` IS A NUMBER
`form 46 the duty to appear before the court when required` MEANS
    PARTY `the offender`
    MUST `form 46 appear before the court`
    WITHIN `the days within which the court requires the offender to appear`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the offender` BECAUSE "the offender did not appear before the court when required to do so by the court"

@ref Form 46 (Section 732.1) (src:18858)
GIVEN `the days within which the notice must be given` IS A NUMBER
`form 46 the duty to notify the court or probation officer of a change` MEANS
    PARTY `the offender`
    MUST `form 46 notify the court or probation officer of the change`
    WITHIN `the days within which the notice must be given`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the offender` BECAUSE "the offender did not notify the court or probation officer of the change"

§ `Form 47 (Section 462.48) -- Order To Disclose Income Tax Information`

-- src:18863 | FORM 47 (Section 462.48) Order To Disclose Income Tax Information
-- src:18864 | Canada,
-- src:18865 | Province of ,
-- src:18866 | (territorial division).
-- src:18867 | To A.B., of , (office or occupation):
-- src:18868 | Whereas, it appears on the oath of C.D., of , that there are reasonable grounds for believing that E.F., of , has committed or benefited from the commission of the offence of and that the information or documents (describe information or documents) are likely to be of substantial value to an investigation of that offence or a related matter; and
-- src:18869 | Whereas there are reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access to the information or documents, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation if the access is obtained;
-- src:18870 | This is, therefore, to authorize and require you between the hours of (as the judge may direct), during the period commencing on and ending on , to produce all the above-mentioned information and documents to one of the following police officers, namely, (here name police officers) and allow the police officer to remove the information or documents, or to allow the police officer access to the above-mentioned information and documents and to examine them, as the judge directs, subject to the following conditions (state conditions):
-- src:18871 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18872 | Signature of judge
@ref Form 47 (Section 462.48) (src:18863-18872)
DECLARE `form 47 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 47 produce the information and documents to one of the named police officers`

-- The order rests on the two recitals: on the oath, reasonable grounds to believe that the person named has committed or benefited from the
-- commission of the offence and that the information is likely to be of substantial value; and reasonable grounds to believe that it is in the
-- public interest to allow access, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation.
@ref Form 47 (Section 462.48) (src:18868-18870)
GIVEN `it appears on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that the person named has committed or benefited from the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or documents are likely to be of substantial value to an investigation of that offence or a related matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 47 the order authorizes and requires the addressee to produce the information` MEANS
    IF     `it appears on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that the person named has committed or benefited from the commission of the offence`
       AND `the information or documents are likely to be of substantial value to an investigation of that offence or a related matter`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is, therefore, to authorize and require you": the order rests on the two "Whereas" recitals, and the Form does not say what follows when one is not made out

-- "to produce all the above-mentioned information and documents to one of the following police officers ... between the hours of (as the judge
-- may direct), during the period commencing on and ending on , ... subject to the following conditions": is a production within the order?
-- A bare "must" not done answers JUST FALSE (the duty is not met; fork F5).
@ref Form 47 (Section 462.48) (src:18870)
GIVEN `the information is produced to one of the police officers the order names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the production is between the hours the judge directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the production is during the period the order states` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the production is subject to the conditions the order states` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 47 the production meets the order` MEANS
    IF     `the information is produced to one of the police officers the order names`
       AND `the production is between the hours the judge directed`
       AND `the production is during the period the order states`
       AND `the production is subject to the conditions the order states`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "between the hours of (as the judge may direct), during the period commencing on and ending on , to produce all the above-mentioned information and documents to one of the following police officers ... subject to the following conditions"

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the addressee is "A.B., of , (office or occupation)", taken as a public officer (NEEDS-CORE.md); the deadline is
-- the number of days from the start of the period to its end.
@ref Form 47 (Section 462.48) (src:18867-18870)
GIVEN `the days of the period the order states` IS A NUMBER
`form 47 the duty of the addressee` MEANS
    PARTY `a public officer`
    MUST `form 47 produce the information and documents to one of the named police officers`
    WITHIN `the days of the period the order states`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a public officer` BECAUSE "the addressee did not produce the information and documents within the period the order states"

§ `Form 48 (Section 672.13) -- Assessment Order of the Court`

-- src:18874 | FORM 48 (Section 672.13) Assessment Order of the Court
-- src:18875 | Canada,
-- src:18876 | Province of
-- src:18877 | (territorial division)
-- src:18878 | Whereas I have (or if the signatory is the clerk of the court, the judge or justice has) reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of (name of accused), who has been charged with , may be necessary to determine *
-- src:18879 | [ ] whether the accused is unfit to stand trial
-- src:18880 | [ ] whether the accused suffered from a mental disorder so as to exempt the accused from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1) of the Criminal Code at the time of the act or omission charged against the accused
-- src:18881 | [ ] whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, if the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child
-- src:18882 | [ ] if a verdict of unfit to stand trial or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused, the appropriate disposition to be made in respect of the accused under section 672.54, 672.58 or 672.64 of the Criminal Code or whether the court should, under subsection 672.84(3) of that Act, revoke a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused
-- src:18883 | [ ] if a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused, whether the court should order a stay of proceedings under section 672.851 of the Criminal Code
-- src:18884 | An assessment of the mental condition of (name of accused) is ordered to be conducted by/at (name of person or service by which or place where assessment is to be made) for a period of days.
-- src:18885 | This order is to be in force for a total of days, including travelling time, during which time the accused is to remain *
-- src:18886 | [ ] in custody at (place where accused is to be detained)
-- src:18887 | [ ] out of custody, on the following conditions:
-- src:18888 | (set out conditions, if applicable)
-- src:18889 | Dated (date), at (place).
-- src:18890 | (Signature of judge, provincial court judge, justice or clerk of the court)
@ref Form 48 (Section 672.13) (src:18874-18890)
DECLARE `form 48 the purpose of the assessment` IS ONE OF
    `form 48 purpose 1 whether the accused is unfit to stand trial`
    `form 48 purpose 2 whether the accused suffered from a mental disorder so as to exempt the accused from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)`
    `form 48 purpose 3 whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence`
    `form 48 purpose 4 the appropriate disposition under section 672.54, 672.58 or 672.64, or whether to revoke a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused`
    `form 48 purpose 5 whether the court should order a stay of proceedings under section 672.851`

-- "Whereas I have reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of (name of accused), who has been charged with ,
-- may be necessary to determine" one of five purposes. Purposes 3, 4 and 5 are each introduced by "if" (fork F13).
@ref Form 48 (Section 672.13) (src:18878-18883)
GIVEN purpose IS A `form 48 the purpose of the assessment`
      `the court has reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of the accused may be necessary to determine the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 newly-born child: the child is a newly-born child` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48 the court has grounds to order an assessment for the purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court has reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of the accused may be necessary to determine the purpose`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Whereas I have (or if the signatory is the clerk of the court, the judge or justice has) reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of (name of accused), who has been charged with , may be necessary to determine": the grounds are the premise of the order, and the Form is silent without them
        IF purpose EQUALS `form 48 purpose 1 whether the accused is unfit to stand trial`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF purpose EQUALS `form 48 purpose 2 whether the accused suffered from a mental disorder so as to exempt the accused from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF purpose EQUALS `form 48 purpose 3 whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence`
            THEN
                IF NOT `the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child"
                ELSE `s 2 newly-born child: the child is a newly-born child`
        IF purpose EQUALS `form 48 purpose 4 the appropriate disposition under section 672.54, 672.58 or 672.64, or whether to revoke a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused`
            THEN
                IF `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused` OR `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a verdict of unfit to stand trial or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused"
        OTHERWISE
            IF `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused, whether the court should order a stay of proceedings under section 672.851"

-- "This order is to be in force for a total of ___ days, including travelling time": in force on the day if the day is within the total
-- number of days from the day of the order (a period the text fixes in its own words: outside it, JUST FALSE; fork F14).
@ref Form 48 (Section 672.13) (src:18884-18885)
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE
      `the total number of days the order is in force, including travelling time` IS A NUMBER
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48 the order is in force` MEANS
    IF `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the day asked about` `the date of the order` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, `the total number of days the order is in force, including travelling time`, FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This order is to be in force for a total of days, including travelling time"

DECLARE `form 48 the accused's status during the order` IS ONE OF
    `form 48 in custody at the place named`
    `form 48 out of custody, on the conditions set out`

-- "during which time the accused is to remain [ ] in custody at (place) [ ] out of custody, on the following conditions": one box is ticked.
@ref Form 48 (Section 672.13) (src:18885-18888)
GIVEN `the box ticked` IS A `form 48 the accused's status during the order`
      `the status asked about` IS A `form 48 the accused's status during the order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48 the accused is to remain in custody or out of custody` MEANS
    IF `the box ticked` EQUALS `the status asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the accused is to remain * ... in custody at (place where accused is to be detained) ... out of custody, on the following conditions": two alternatives, one ticked; the Form says nothing of the one not ticked

@ref Form 48 (Section 672.13) (src:18886-18888)
GIVEN `the box ticked` IS A `form 48 the accused's status during the order`
      `the condition is one the order sets out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48 the accused must comply with the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the box ticked` EQUALS `form 48 out of custody, on the conditions set out`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "out of custody, on the following conditions": the conditions belong to the out-of-custody alternative
        IF `the condition is one the order sets out`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the following conditions: (set out conditions, if applicable)"

§ `Form 48.1 (Section 672.13) -- Assessment Order of the Review Board`

-- src:18892 | FORM 48.1 (Section 672.13) Assessment Order of the Review Board
-- src:18893 | Canada,
-- src:18894 | Province of
-- src:18895 | (territorial division)
-- src:18896 | Whereas I have reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of (name of accused), who has been charged with , may be necessary to *
-- src:18897 | [ ] if a verdict of unfit to stand trial or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused, make a disposition under section 672.54 of the Criminal Code or determine whether the Review Board should, under subsection 672.84(1) of that Act, refer to the superior court of criminal jurisdiction for review a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused
-- src:18898 | [ ] if a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused, determine whether the Review Board should make a recommendation to the court that has jurisdiction in respect of the offence charged against the accused to hold an inquiry to determine whether a stay of proceedings should be ordered in accordance with section 672.851 of the Criminal Code
-- src:18899 | I hereby order an assessment of the mental condition of (name of accused) to be conducted by/at (name of person or service by whom or place where assessment is to be made) for a period of days.
-- src:18900 | This order is to be in force for a total of days, including travelling time, during which time the accused is to remain *
-- src:18901 | [ ] in custody at (place where accused is to be detained)
-- src:18902 | [ ] out of custody, on the following conditions:
-- src:18903 | (set out conditions, if applicable)
-- src:18904 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18905 | (Signature of Chairperson of the Review Board)
@ref Form 48.1 (Section 672.13) (src:18892-18905)
DECLARE `form 48.1 the purpose of the assessment` IS ONE OF
    `form 48.1 purpose 1 to make a disposition under section 672.54 or determine whether to refer a high-risk finding for review under subsection 672.84(1)`
    `form 48.1 purpose 2 to determine whether to recommend an inquiry into a stay of proceedings under section 672.851`

@ref Form 48.1 (Section 672.13) (src:18896-18898)
GIVEN purpose IS A `form 48.1 the purpose of the assessment`
      `the Review Board has reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of the accused may be necessary for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48.1 the Review Board has grounds to order an assessment for the purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Review Board has reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of the accused may be necessary for the purpose`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Whereas I have reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of the mental condition of (name of accused), who has been charged with , may be necessary to": the grounds are the premise of the order
        IF purpose EQUALS `form 48.1 purpose 1 to make a disposition under section 672.54 or determine whether to refer a high-risk finding for review under subsection 672.84(1)`
            THEN
                IF `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused` OR `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a verdict of unfit to stand trial or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused"
        OTHERWISE
            IF `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused"

@ref Form 48.1 (Section 672.13) (src:18899-18900)
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE
      `the total number of days the order is in force, including travelling time` IS A NUMBER
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48.1 the order is in force` MEANS
    IF `forms 24-54 the day falls within a period that begins on a day` `the day asked about` `the date of the order` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, `the total number of days the order is in force, including travelling time`, FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This order is to be in force for a total of days, including travelling time"

DECLARE `form 48.1 the accused's status during the order` IS ONE OF
    `form 48.1 in custody at the place named`
    `form 48.1 out of custody, on the conditions set out`

@ref Form 48.1 (Section 672.13) (src:18900-18903)
GIVEN `the box ticked` IS A `form 48.1 the accused's status during the order`
      `the status asked about` IS A `form 48.1 the accused's status during the order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48.1 the accused is to remain in custody or out of custody` MEANS
    IF `the box ticked` EQUALS `the status asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the accused is to remain * ... in custody at (place where accused is to be detained) ... out of custody, on the following conditions": two alternatives, one ticked

@ref Form 48.1 (Section 672.13) (src:18901-18903)
GIVEN `the box ticked` IS A `form 48.1 the accused's status during the order`
      `the condition is one the order sets out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48.1 the accused must comply with the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the box ticked` EQUALS `form 48.1 out of custody, on the conditions set out`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "out of custody, on the following conditions": the conditions belong to the out-of-custody alternative
        IF `the condition is one the order sets out`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the following conditions: (set out conditions, if applicable)"

§ `Form 51 -- Notice of Obligation To Provide Samples of Bodily Substance`

-- src:18989 | FORM 51 (Paragraphs 732.1(3)(c.2), 742.3(2)(a.2), 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.03(7)(h), 810.011(6)(f), 810.1(3.02)(i) and 810.2(4.1)(g)) Notice of Obligation To Provide Samples of Bodily Substance
-- src:18990 | To A.B., of , (occupation), (address in Canada), (date of birth), (gender):
-- src:18991 | Because, on (date), you were ordered, under (applicable provision) of the Criminal Code, to provide samples of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals for the purpose of analysis;
-- src:18992 | You are provided with this notice to inform you of your obligations with respect to providing samples.
-- src:18993 | 1 On (specify a day not earlier than 24 hours after the day on which the notice is served), you must report, at any time from (time) to (time), at (address of place at which sample to be taken, as designated by the Attorney General of the province or Minister of Justice of the territory), to provide a sample of your (specify type of bodily substance prescribed by regulation).
-- src:18994 | 2 Every (specify a number not less than seven) days after you first report to provide a sample, you must report, at any time from (time) to (time), at (address of place at which sample to be taken, as designated by the Attorney General of the province or Minister of Justice of the territory), to provide a sample of your (specify type of bodily substance prescribed by regulation).
-- src:18995 | 3 You have the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation to provide samples, and the right to appeal any decision of that court.
-- src:18996 | 4 If you are found to have not complied with your obligation to provide samples as set out in this notice, you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both (or, in the case of a conditional sentence, you may be subject to proceedings under section 742.6 of the Criminal Code, the consequences of which may include imprisonment).
-- src:18997 | 5 The results of the analysis of the bodily substances may be used or disclosed in accordance with the Criminal Code, including in proceedings against you, the result of which may be that you are subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both (or, in the case of a conditional sentence, including in proceedings under section 742.6 of the Criminal Code, the consequences of which may include imprisonment).
-- src:18998 | Served on (date), at (place the notice is served).
-- src:18999 | (Signature of probation officer, supervisor or person designated by the Attorney General or Minister of Justice, as the case may be)
@ref Form 51 (Paragraphs 732.1(3)(c.2), 742.3(2)(a.2), 810(3.02)(c), 810.01(4.1)(g), 810.03(7)(h), 810.011(6)(f), 810.1(3.02)(i) and 810.2(4.1)(g)) (src:18989-18999)
DECLARE `form 51 the consequence of not complying` IS ONE OF
    `form 51 a fine or imprisonment, or both`
    `form 51 proceedings under section 742.6, the consequences of which may include imprisonment`
    `form 51 the notice states no consequence, the person not having been found to have failed to comply`

-- "Because, on (date), you were ordered, under (applicable provision) of the Criminal Code, to provide samples of a bodily substance
-- prescribed by regulation at regular intervals for the purpose of analysis": the obligation the notice informs the person of.
@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18991-18992)
GIVEN `the person was ordered to provide samples of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals for the purpose of analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 51 the person is subject to the obligation to provide samples` MEANS
    IF `the person was ordered to provide samples of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals for the purpose of analysis`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Because, on (date), you were ordered ... to provide samples ...; You are provided with this notice to inform you of your obligations": the notice is addressed to a person so ordered

-- Paragraph 1: "On (specify a day not earlier than 24 hours after the day on which the notice is served), you must report". Fork F15: the day must
-- be at least one calendar day after the day of service (the other reading counts 24 hours from the moment of service, which a date cannot show).
@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18993)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice is served` IS A DATE
      `the first reporting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 51 para 1 the first report is on a permitted day` MEANS
    IF `the first reporting day` AT LEAST (`the day on which the notice is served` PLUS 1)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "specify a day not earlier than 24 hours after the day on which the notice is served"

-- "you must report, at any time from (time) to (time), at (address of place ...)": the minute of the day of the report lies from the first time to the second, both included.
@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18993)
GIVEN `the minute of the day at which the person reports` IS A NUMBER
      `the first minute of the day the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
      `the last minute of the day the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 51 para 1 the person reports within the hours stated` MEANS
    IF `the minute of the day at which the person reports` AT LEAST `the first minute of the day the notice allows`
       AND `the minute of the day at which the person reports` AT MOST `the last minute of the day the notice allows`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "you must report, at any time from (time) to (time)"

-- Paragraph 2: "Every (specify a number not less than seven) days after you first report to provide a sample, you must report".
@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18994)
GIVEN `the number of days stated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 51 para 2 the number of days stated is permitted` MEANS
    IF `the number of days stated` AT LEAST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every (specify a number not less than seven) days after you first report"

@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18994)
GIVEN `the first reporting day` IS A DATE
      `the number of days stated` IS A NUMBER
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 51 para 2 the person must report on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of days stated` LESS THAN 7
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every (specify a number not less than seven) days": a notice stating fewer than seven days is outside the Form
        IF `the day asked about` AT MOST `the first reporting day`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every (specify a number not less than seven) days after you first report to provide a sample"
        IF ((Day `the day asked about`) MINUS (Day `the first reporting day`)) MODULO `the number of days stated` EQUALS 0
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every (specify a number not less than seven) days after you first report to provide a sample"

-- Paragraph 3: "You have the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation to provide samples, and the right to appeal any decision of that court."
@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18995)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 51 para 3 the person may apply to terminate the obligation` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "You have the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation to provide samples": the right is the person's who is given the notice

@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18995)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has decided an application to terminate the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 51 para 3 the person may appeal the decision` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to the notice` AND `a court has decided an application to terminate the obligation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the right to appeal any decision of that court": the right is to appeal a decision of the court on the application

-- Paragraph 4: "If you are found to have not complied with your obligation to provide samples as set out in this notice, you may be subject to
-- a fine or imprisonment, or to both (or, in the case of a conditional sentence, you may be subject to proceedings under section 742.6 of the
-- Criminal Code, the consequences of which may include imprisonment)." JUST means "may be subject to": a liability, not a certainty.
@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18996)
GIVEN `the person is found to have not complied with the obligation to provide samples` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is part of a conditional sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `form 51 the consequence of not complying`
`form 51 para 4 the consequence of not complying` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is found to have not complied with the obligation to provide samples`
            THEN JUST `form 51 the notice states no consequence, the person not having been found to have failed to comply`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you are found to have not complied with your obligation to provide samples as set out in this notice"
        IF `the obligation is part of a conditional sentence`
            THEN JUST `form 51 proceedings under section 742.6, the consequences of which may include imprisonment`
        OTHERWISE JUST `form 51 a fine or imprisonment, or both`

-- Paragraph 5: "The results of the analysis of the bodily substances may be used or disclosed in accordance with the Criminal Code, including in
-- proceedings against you".
@ref Form 51 (Section 732.1) (src:18997)
GIVEN `the use or disclosure is in accordance with the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 51 para 5 the results of the analysis may be used in proceedings against the person` MEANS
    IF `the use or disclosure is in accordance with the Criminal Code`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be used or disclosed in accordance with the Criminal Code": a use outside the Code is not covered
